 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Low Texture/Repetitive Patterns:** Classical SfM fails here due to few keypoints [S1]. VMRF avoids this by not relying on SfM [S1].
-*   **Out-of-Dataset Views:** GNeRF's inversion network is disturbed by views beyond the training dataset if the accurate pose distribution is unavailable [S1]. VMRF mitigates this by using relative pose estimation via view matching [S1].
-*   **Occlusion:** Causes inconsistent total mass between source and target feature distributions [S1]. Standard Optimal Transport fails by matching outliers [S1]. VMRF uses Unbalanced OT (UOT) with KL divergence penalties to handle this [S1].
+*   **Low Texture/Repetitive Patterns:** Classical SfM fails here due to few keypoints [S1].
+*   **Out-of-Dataset Views:** GNeRF's inversion network is disturbed by views beyond the training dataset if the accurate pose distribution is unavailable [S1].
+*   **Occlusion:** Causes inconsistent total mass between source and target feature distributions. Standard Optimal Transport fails by matching outliers [S1].
 
